      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree, some projects of mine was nerfed, or broken entirely by some restrictions (Though I found some new ways to enhance the chatbox, made it look nicer while keeping the chatbox small in height for my bot/AI's chatbox) but it still makes it difficult to achieve what I want to do.\n\nThe extreme chatbox spams should probably be manually reviewed for certain users who may legitimately need fast chatboxes in extreme rare scenarios (both you and I know this, it's already tedious enough).\n\nIn my own OSC library I've developed (private, don't ask) I literally had to put my own specialized rate limit to ensure I can update the chatbox as frequently as possible while also not getting bonked for spam.\n\nAnd I would love to mute chatboxes and mics individually, I've been in way too many scenarios where I want to talk to a mute player but I don't want to hear their music blasting at 5000% volume where even setting the volume to 5% isn't even sufficient. I guess earmuff mode is a thing but that defeats the purpose entirely if you can't hear anyone.\n\nYou know this already but I've already worked out what I can and can't do to a chatbox, even beyond intended limits, so I can help you out to some extent.\n\nAs for clearing the chatbox, It's weird as while you can clear the chatbox *while* you're rate limited, I don't get why it counts towards it anyway.\n\nI understand it may be throwned upon by a good handful of users but there's just the select few cases where it could be considered accepted, depending on the scenario.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
