  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Right now when developing software for Celeste-AI and or any other bot creations a lot of us developers use ChatBubbles to help dictate actions and or express information to users, especially hard of hearing people, they've been increasingly becoming more and more of a hassle to support because they keep having more restrictions put on them.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/RyMXKU3mfOU?si=lGrwsa9iwUUQPFmI \n\nExample of using them properly, I timed it very specifically but if I'm not careful they stop working for 30s which completely breaks the flow of chats and or user experience drops a ton.\n\nI propose that instead of nerfing chatbubbles more, instead a more developer friendly approach is used that allows users to stop malicious actors abusing the chatbubbles but not making it harder to use them in development.\n\n* Lower Chat restrictions, leave some but 5-10 messages every few seconds shouldn't trip the 30s cooldown so often, that should be reserved for extreme cases where someone is sending 1000's every second, there's no scenario where you need to do it that often.\n\n* Resetting chatbubbles with \"\" should not count towards the ratelimit.\n\n* Add proper safeguards for people actually abusing similar to MIC spam users, we players should decide if something is actually being abused in these scenarios, IE being able to mute players chat bubbles individually or if its a group instance maybe they can force their text bubbles off.",
